# D10(a) NEGATIVE (decisions.md, ratified 2026-07-06): a local `&`-bind must
# not dodge the rejection by hiding in a `do:` block whose TAIL value is a
# borrow (`do:` newline, then `&a`). The check recurses the block's tail
# statement. ⚠ The MULTI-LINE `do:` form is mandatory — the inline `do: &a`
# shorthand is a parse error and would "pass" for the wrong reason. Pre-D10
# this ACCEPTED and wrote through (the bind aliased `a`, printed `4/4`).
# Expected: error[E_LocalBorrowBind] at the initializer.
void main():
    Vector[int] a = [1, 2, 3]
    auto r = do:
        &a
    r.push(9)
    print(r.len())
